# tools/aws/burst.env.example — every variable tools/aws/burst.sh reads (M15.4).
# Copy to tools/aws/burst.env (gitignored) or export in the shell; no value here is
# a recommendation. Credentials never go in a file in this repository: the AWS CLI's
# own configuration (`aws configure`, or a named profile) is what the script uses,
# and the Tiingo key never reaches the box at all — the archive's bars go up as data.
#
# REGION            the AWS region; default: the CLI's configured region
# INSTANCE_TYPES    spot instance types, tried in order; default: "c7a.32xlarge c6i.32xlarge"
# CONFIG            the programme's configuration (gitignored); default: configs/programme-2.toml
# REGISTER          the programme's Register the box reads; default: register/programme-2.jsonl
# NAME              the prefix of every AWS resource the burst creates; default: occams-burst
#
# Everything else is derived: the bucket name from the account, the subnets from the
# default VPC (created if the region has none), the instance role and the launch
# template from NAME. `setup` creates them; `teardown --all` removes every one.
#
# REGION=
# INSTANCE_TYPES=
# CONFIG=configs/programme-N.toml
# REGISTER=register/programme-N.jsonl
# NAME=
